      "key": {
        "uuid": "9df37c62_4aa745f9",
        "filename": "src/ports/SkImageEncoder_NDK.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 50,
      "author": {
        "id": 5020
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-26T20:49:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So doesn\u0027t that mean on older devices that we will load in libjnigraphics and keep it loaded even if it doesn\u0027t have the symbol that we need?  It seems more memory efficient to keep the memory mapped only if we will be using it instead of keeping it around when we hit the error case as well.  Do we anticipate hitting the error case in any of our clients?\n\nIf we do keep it as is can you cadd a comment above dlclose that we can remove this handle because we used RTLD_NODELETE?",
      "parentUuid": "484ff1fe_be525f58",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 50,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 50,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "447e1133e8fd161ba0b019d75a0a3126a602d057",
